{"language_code":"eng","language_probability":0.9490225315093994,"text":"The Birkin is your dream bag, and that's the problem. So here are five bags you should buy instead. Number five, Bottega Veneta. No logo anywhere, the weave does the talking, and only the right people can read it from across the room. Number four, the Margaux from The Row. This is the fashion insider's Birkin. Same soft shape, no hardware, and the waiting list quietly moved here. Number three, Valextra. Milan, 1937, the quiet one. Clean lines, none of the flair, and the Easy Day has been its icon since twenty eleven. Number two, Delvaux. Brussels, eighteen twenty-nine. It calls itself the oldest fine leather house in the world, and it will sell you its best bag on a Tuesday. No wait list, no games. And number one, the Birkin-inspired one almost nobody has heard of yet, and the one I actually pre-ordered. This is the Vivienne from Valentra. Same silhouette, the belted brass turn lock, vegetable tanned leather all the way through, braided leather trim, and no logo anywhere. It's soft, so it slouches and molds to you instead of sitting stiff on your arm. It comes in four colors. It's twenty-five percent off on pre-order right now, one forty-nine instead of one ninety-nine, and the first run ships in October. I left the link below.","words":[{"text":"The","start":0.079,"end":0.159,"type":"word","logprob":-1.4305104514278355e-6},{"text":" ","start":0.159,"end":0.199,"type":"spacing","logprob":-0.0003843760641757399},{"text":"Birkin","start":0.199,"end":0.719,"type":"word","logprob":-0.00019844648068101378},{"text":" ","start":0.719,"end":0.799,"type":"spacing","logprob":-2.3841855067985307e-7},{"text":"is","start":0.799,"end":1.079,"type":"word","logprob":-2.3841855067985307e-7},{"text":" ","start":1.079,"end":1.279,"type":"spacing","logprob":0.0},{"text":"your","start":1.279,"end":1.419,"type":"word","logprob":0.0},{"text":" ","start":1.419,"end":1.519,"type":"spacing","logprob":-7.152555099310121e